---

<p class="section__intro">In an emergency, getting reliable information quickly is crucial. Knowing where to turn before an incident happens means you won't waste time searching when it matters most.</p>

<div class="alert-box alert-box--danger">
  <p class="alert-box__heading">In an emergency, call 999.</p>
  <p>This page provides information on receiving warnings and alerts. If you are in immediate danger, call 999 immediately.</p>
</div>

<div class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__heading">GBC Radio — Primary Emergency Broadcast</h2>
  <p><strong>GBC Radio is Gibraltar's primary source of official emergency information.</strong> In a major emergency, the Gibraltar Broadcasting Corporation will broadcast continuous updates and instructions from official authorities.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>FM:</strong> 91.3 FM</li>
    <li><strong>AM (MW):</strong> 1458 AM</li>
    <li>GBC Radio can be received on a standard battery-powered or wind-up radio — this works even during power cuts and mobile network congestion.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="alert-box alert-box--info">
    <p class="alert-box__heading">Why radio matters</p>
    <p>During a major emergency, mobile networks may be congested, internet access may be unreliable, and power cuts may affect devices. A battery-powered or wind-up radio is the most resilient way to receive official emergency information. Include one in your emergency grab bag.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__heading">HM Government of Gibraltar — Official Channels</h2>
  <p>HM Government of Gibraltar issues official emergency statements and public guidance via:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Official website:</strong> <a href="https://www.gibraltar.gov.gi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.gibraltar.gov.gi<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
    <li><strong>Social media:</strong> Follow @GibGov on official social media platforms for real-time updates.</li>
    <li>Government press releases and emergency notices are also published via the Gibraltar Chronicle and GBC online.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__heading">Royal Gibraltar Police (RGP)</h2>
  <p>The RGP provides public safety information and warnings via:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Social media:</strong> Follow @RGPolice for public safety notices, road closures, and emergency warnings.</li>
    <li><strong>Non-emergency line:</strong> <a href="tel:20072500">200 72500</a></li>
    <li><strong>Emergency:</strong> 999</li>
  </ul>
  <p>During incidents, the RGP may issue instructions via loudhailer, door-to-door, and through official social media and GBC Radio.</p>
</div>

<div class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__heading">Civil Contingencies Unit</h2>
  <p>The Civil Contingencies Unit (CCU) coordinates Gibraltar's emergency response and issues public guidance during major incidents. CCU information is issued through HM Government of Gibraltar channels during emergencies. This website — <strong>Emergency Preparedness</strong> — is published by HM Government of Gibraltar as a preparedness resource.</p>
</div>


<div class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__heading">Weather Warnings</h2>
  <p>The Gibraltar Meteorological Office issues weather warnings for severe conditions affecting Gibraltar and the surrounding area.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Weather warnings are issued on the Gibraltar Meteorological Office website and shared via HM Government of Gibraltar social media.</li>
    <li>Warnings use a colour-coded system (Yellow / Amber / Red) indicating the severity and likelihood of dangerous weather.</li>
    <li>Always act on weather warnings — particularly Red warnings, which indicate an immediate threat to life.</li>
    <li>For specific weather-related hazard guidance, see the <a href="/hazards/">Hazards</a> section.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__heading">Stay Safe Online</h2>
  <p>During emergencies, misinformation spreads rapidly on social media. Protect yourself and others:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Only share information from verified official sources: HM Government of Gibraltar, RGP, GHA, and GBC.</li>
    <li>If you are unsure whether information is accurate, do not share it.</li>
    <li>Check official accounts directly rather than relying on shared posts — these may be outdated or altered.</li>
    <li>If you see dangerous misinformation circulating, report it to the RGP on 200 72500.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
